Implement a standard-library-only command dispatcher for an in-memory workshop in `solution.rs`.

Expose this exact API:

```rust
use std::collections::BTreeMap;

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Tool { pub id: u64, pub name: String, pub zone: String }
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]
pub struct Workshop {
    pub name: String,
    pub zones: BTreeMap<String, Vec<u64>>,
    pub tools: BTreeMap<u64, Tool>,
}
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Command {
    Health, Summary, Zone(String), AddZone(String), RemoveZone(String),
    Tool(u64), AddTool { id: u64, name: String, zone: String }, RemoveTool(u64),
}
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Reply { Text(String), Changed, NotFound, Conflict, Invalid }

pub fn dispatch(workshop: &mut Workshop, command: Command) -> Reply;
```

Zone names and tool names are valid only when nonempty after trimming. Store their trimmed forms. `Health` returns `Text("ready")`. `Summary` returns the workshop name followed by zone names in sorted map order as `name|zone1,zone2`; an empty zone list leaves the text after `|` empty. `Zone` returns comma-separated tool IDs in insertion order. `Tool` returns `id|name|zone`.

Adding an existing zone or tool ID returns `Conflict`. Adding a tool requires an existing zone. Removing a zone must also remove all tools assigned to it. Removing a tool must remove its ID from its zone. Successful mutations return `Changed`; malformed names return `Invalid`; missing lookups or removals return `NotFound`. Lookup strings are trimmed but otherwise case-sensitive. Failed commands must not mutate state. Expose no `main` function.

